  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I verified TX-0401 in your records (account ACC-1005):\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Type:** Outgoing card payment, status settled\n\nThe account also shows another EUR 240.00 card payment to TechMart Online on 2026-07-14 (TX-0402), so the two charges match in amount and merchant.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes available, with what each would cover:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** The same purchase was charged more than once. The TX-0401 and TX-0402 pair may fit this.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** A debit was taken from your account without your permission.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** Your card details were used without your authority in an online or phone transaction, without the physical card.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid for goods that were never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nWhich of these applies depends on what happened. Tell me, and I can check whether the transaction is eligible under that code before anything is filed. I will not open a dispute without your confirmation.",
